invariant: INV-14
file: tls.c
catches: webpki_session_test
reason: ch_connect stops holding an offered protocol name to
  CH_ALPN_NAME_MAX bytes, so a longer name passes the config check and
  the ClientHello grows past the CH_HELLO_MAX the TX staging array is
  sized for. The hello then fails to build and the session dies with
  CH_ECAP mid-handshake instead of CH_EINVAL at the config.
  bin/webpki_session_test's name-length boundary rows object.

--- old
    return protocol->name != NULL && protocol->name_len > 0 &&
           protocol->name_len <= CH_ALPN_NAME_MAX;
--- new
    return protocol->name != NULL && protocol->name_len > 0;
